# Vector-3D: a 3-component 32-bit-float vector. Pure float math, identical on every backend. The combiners are named `plus` / `minus` because `add` / `subtract` are the number arithmetic primitives. `scale` multiplies by a scalar, `dot` is the scalar product, `cross` the vector product, `length` the magnitude, `normalize` the unit vector, `distance` the gap between two points.

load @term/seed/code/float
  find square-root

form vector-3
  link x, like decimal
  link y, like decimal
  link z, like decimal

  task plus
    take self
    take other, like vector-3
    like vector-3
    send back
      make vector-3
        bind x
          call add
            read self/x
            read other/x
        bind y
          call add
            read self/y
            read other/y
        bind z
          call add
            read self/z
            read other/z

  task minus
    take self
    take other, like vector-3
    like vector-3
    send back
      make vector-3
        bind x
          call subtract
            read self/x
            read other/x
        bind y
          call subtract
            read self/y
            read other/y
        bind z
          call subtract
            read self/z
            read other/z

  task scale
    take self
    take factor, like decimal
    like vector-3
    send back
      make vector-3
        bind x
          call multiply
            read self/x
            read factor
        bind y
          call multiply
            read self/y
            read factor
        bind z
          call multiply
            read self/z
            read factor

  task dot
    take self
    take other, like vector-3
    like decimal
    send back
      call add
        call add
          call multiply
            read self/x
            read other/x
          call multiply
            read self/y
            read other/y
        call multiply
          read self/z
          read other/z

  task cross
    take self
    take other, like vector-3
    like vector-3
    send back
      make vector-3
        bind x
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read self/y
              read other/z
            call multiply
              read self/z
              read other/y
        bind y
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read self/z
              read other/x
            call multiply
              read self/x
              read other/z
        bind z
          call subtract
            call multiply
              read self/x
              read other/y
            call multiply
              read self/y
              read other/x

  task length
    take self
    like decimal
    send back
      call square-root
        call dot
          read self
          read self

  task normalize
    take self
    like vector-3
    save magnitude
      call length
        read self
    send back
      make vector-3
        bind x
          call divide
            read self/x
            read magnitude
        bind y
          call divide
            read self/y
            read magnitude
        bind z
          call divide
            read self/z
            read magnitude

  task distance
    take self
    take other, like vector-3
    like decimal
    send back
      call length
        call minus
          read self
          read other

task make-vector-3
  take x, like decimal
  take y, like decimal
  take z, like decimal
  like vector-3
  send back
    make vector-3
      bind x, read x
      bind y, read y
      bind z, read z
